  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-04-06T20:48:05.503Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "In the VRC Avatars SDK 3.1.13, a new pre-build error was added for audio clips that have \"Decompress On Load\" enabled, but \"Load In Background\" disabled, telling the user that \"Load In Background\" must be enabled for this case. \n\nHowever, the error only has a \"Select\" button, which takes the user to the audio source, not the clip itself, requiring an additional clickthrough. This has caused some confusion among users, who don't always recognize how to get to the audio clip and change the setting. \n\nIt seems to be a trivial import option change and reimport, so it should have an auto fix button that applies the option to all problematic audio clips, similar to the \"Streaming Mipmaps\" auto-fix.",
